    <GaugingStation location="Drakelow Park" name="Trent" number="28019">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station with complex rating history owing to river regrading in 1965 and 1973 draining a very large catchment that contains urban and industrial land use.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Complex rating history owing to river re-grading (1965 and 1973). Multiple peak flow ratings, particularly since 2001. High flow precision limited by ungauged flow over the left bank. Much storage in valley gravels. A number of gaugings have been taken to assess out of bank flows; on 1/11/2000 gaugings taken at 3.216mASD showed floodplain flow to be 26% of the total flow of 252m3/s. Extreme high flow gaugings carried out across the floodplain and main river section in Burton-upon-Trent, from St. Peters Bridge using a remote controlled ADCP. In-channel weed growth at the station can affect low and medium flow gaugings.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station. The left bank is a low lying golf course that is inundated from 2.68mASD. Cableway removed in 2014 - flow gaugings still performed in old cableway section.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Summer flows reprocessed in 2010 for the period 2006-2010 to account for weed growth. 2011 flows reprocessed to account for severe weed growth. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in October 2018 (WINFAP Files v7). The majority of low flows (~&lt;15 m3/s) between 16 July - 30 September 2018 are flagged as suspect.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Flows substantially modified, particularly by imports into the Tame system.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Very large catchment. Small areas of Coal Measures in the Stoke area. Approx 25% of the catchment is overlain by Boulder Clay and 10% by valley gravel, terraces and alluvium. Drift free areas mostly Triassic Mudstones and Triassic and Permian Sandstones. A large area of the catchment is urban with large urban industrial areas, otherwise, the main land use is mixed farming.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">PGE</Comment>
        </Comments>
